course: dictionary
lesson: 1831
title: One word, many coats
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives four meanings for coat, and the words around it show which one you need. «Put your coat on, it is cold outside.» Here a coat is a warm piece of clothing with sleeves that you wear over your other clothes.
explain: «Donkey coats are not waterproof like horses' coats, so donkeys need shelter from the rain.» Here coat means an animal's fur or hair. The clue is the animals: donkeys and horses have coats, and an animal's coat keeps it warm and protected.
explain: «A shiny glaze, which is a thin coat of glass, makes a mug waterproof.» Here coat means a thin layer spread over a surface. Coat can also be a verb, which means to cover something with a thin layer. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Coat is a noun (a coat, coats) and also a verb (to coat, coating).
fact: As a noun, a coat is a warm piece of clothing with sleeves that you wear over your other clothes when you go outside.
fact: An animal's coat is its fur or hair. Many animals grow a thicker coat before winter and shed it in spring.
fact: A coat can also be a thin layer of paint or another liquid over a surface, like «a second coat» on a fence.
fact: As a verb, to coat something means to cover it with a thin layer, as in «coat the chicken in breadcrumbs».
exercise: «Put your coat on, it is cold outside.» What is a coat here? | *A warm piece of clothing you wear over your other clothes | An animal's fur | A thin layer of paint on a fence | A hat
exercise: «Donkey coats are not waterproof like horses' coats.» What does coat mean here? | A piece of clothing | A layer of paint | *Fur or hair on an animal | To cover something
exercise: What does coat mean in «coat the chicken in breadcrumbs»? | A warm jacket | Fur on an animal | To hang up | *To cover with a thin layer
test: «A shiny glaze, which is a thin coat of glass, makes a mug waterproof.» What does coat mean here? | To hang up | *A thin layer over a surface | An animal's fur | A warm piece of clothing
test: «In Siberia the tame foxes got floppy ears and patchy coats.» What is a patchy coat? | A warm jacket with patches | A thin layer of glass | *Fur or hair that grows in patches | A coat of paint that is uneven
exam: «She wore a long black coat in the rain.» What does coat mean here? | To cover something with paint | A thin layer of glass | *A warm piece of clothing with sleeves | Fur or hair on an animal
